# Import meshes, skeletons, physics assets, and animations correctly

Import meshes, skeletons, physics assets, and animations correctly.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Import meshes, skeletons, physics assets, and animations correctly.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

Open work migrated from the canonical TODO. Add implementation and
validation evidence here as the task advances.

The persistent port preview also exercises both reviewed mesh import paths.
`l1z1` is saved as a native Static Mesh, while Cletus and `sedana` are saved as
Skeletal Meshes with newly created Skeleton companions. The vehicle import
intentionally does not synthesize a Physics Asset, materials, wheel definitions,
or Chaos construction from incomplete evidence; those remain separate typed
construction work rather than manual editor repair.

Vehicle package coverage is now explicit. The generated package index contains
89 `cars` packages: 88 map one-to-one to dedicated vehicle FBXs, while
`extracted-art-cars-common` is the sole shared support package. The specialized
FBX therefore supplies verified presentation geometry without pretending to
replace the package's remaining texture, material, physics, and runtime
semantics.

September 5 scale investigation identified a native-import defect rather than an
FBX geometry defect. The original runtime initializes simulation with
`MetersUnits`, and the repository FBX writers correctly declare
`UnitScaleFactor=100` and `OriginalUnitScaleFactor=100`, meaning one authored
unit is one meter. Unreal Engine 5.8.1 uses centimeters and its FBX asset-import
data defaults `bConvertSceneUnit` to false. The project importer had inherited
that default, so meter-authored coordinates were interpreted numerically as
centimeters and preview meshes arrived one hundred times too small.

`SharImportEditor` now applies one shared FBX scene-unit policy to static,
world, and skeletal imports: `ImportUniformScale=1.0` with
`bConvertSceneUnit=true`.
The policy compiles against the installed Unreal Engine 5.8.1 source/toolchain
and is covered for both static and skeletal import-data paths. The already saved
`PortPreview` assets were imported by the old loaded editor module and therefore
remain scale-invalid until they are reimported after that module is reloaded.
Manual actor scaling is inspection-only and is not accepted as conversion
evidence.

September 5 presentation work adds a separate normalized base-color PNG import
boundary beside the existing FBX/WAV/media imports. It is intentionally not a
catch-all texture policy: it creates exactly one generated-root `Texture2D`,
disables implicit Material creation and replacement, and leaves saving to the
outer transaction. World catalog v8 supplies the material-to-texture relation;
blend, culling, emission, glass, and other material behavior remain owned by the
material projection layer rather than the byte importer.

Vehicle catalog v7 now carries the source-physics boundary forward without
synthesizing target collision. Every decoded vehicle collision and physics
member remains byte-exact, while 137 same-name source rigs additionally publish
1,118 bone-resolved sphere, oriented-box, and cylinder primitives in
`source-bone-local` meter space with Pure3D f32 numeric semantics. A complete
88-vehicle replay retained 274 verbatim sidecars, and an independent audit
matched every sidecar and every recipe back to normalized source evidence.

The Unreal catalog verifier now validates sidecars and recipes fail-closed while
continuing to promote only verified FBX presentation evidence. `prepare-unreal`
projects supported recipes into the imported bone-local frame, and the editor
native kernel now constructs and reads back an unsaved transient Physics Asset
against the real scene-unit `sedana` Skeletal Mesh. That representative test
retains `sedanA` as root zero, accepts Unreal's 16 retained bones from the
19-joint source rig, creates two chassis boxes plus four wheel spheres, and
rejects wrong-scale and malformed geometry.

Generated-root Physics Asset publication now exists as a create-only editor
toolset. The representative `PublishSedana` automation proves the five-body
asset is registered in memory, reads back the expected root/body geometry, marks
the package dirty, and does not save a `.uasset` implicitly. The release-bound
editor-control transaction now also proves explicit save and cold reload for the
real `sedana` Skeletal Mesh, Skeleton, and generated Physics Asset: a fresh
Unreal
process reads all three back with their expected classes and `dirty=false`, and
the saved file hashes survive the restart unchanged. Binding those reviewed
assets into production vehicle construction remains open work.

Vehicle catalog v8 now closes the material-slot handoff ambiguity without
synthesizing target materials. A fresh 88-vehicle replay publishes 1,029 exact
FBX material slots and independently verifies every referenced shader and
texture artifact by size and SHA-256. `sedana` has eight ordered slots,
including glass and light-emitter variants derived by the same planner used by
FBX serialization.

The Unreal catalog verifier requires the slot count to match the FBX summary and
rechecks shader schema and identity. Native `MaterialInstance` creation remains
open work.
